WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.220
Imagine you have a week's worth of inspections, or one big site that

2
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.060
took several days to get round.

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:09.820
Either way, you'll want one record that brings them all together.

4
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.020
On the Check's Record page, press Combine.

5
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:16.680
Then click the records you want, by subject or by person.

6
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.760
Take a group, and everything in it comes as well.

7
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:23.120
Quickler then makes them into one combined record, kept under

8
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.240
Combined Records on that page.

9
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.480
If the records are all from the same place, like a daily check of

10
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.900
one building, the latest answer counts.

11
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.300
If they're from different places, like separate buildings on a big

12
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.560
site, the worst answer is the one that's flagged, and the fault

13
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.980
always says which place it came from.

14
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:44.100
Any photo that turns up more than once appears only once, and the

15
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.920
combined record lists exactly what it was made from, so you can

16
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.500
always find the originals.

17
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.040
So, whether you need one report for a large site, or one for the

18
00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.350
whole week, It only takes a few clicks.

19
00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.320
Quickler has you covered.
